                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I have added an API version to the service/path/interface, the goal being to provide API stability.  That means the API and its associated service/path/interface names should not change incompatibly, or, if they do, then we will need to fix up all the call sites just like we would if a c++ API (function, class, etc) changed names.\n\nGiven the API stability, a variable seems like an unnecessary indirection, does it not?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "sbmrhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 159,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "John Chung",
                        "email": "john.chung@arm.com",
                        "username": "gtossk2"
                    },
                    "message": "It\u2019s fine. I just think some other functions might use those APIs, so keeping them for consistency by using macro could be beneficial."
                },
                {
                    "file": "sbmrhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 160,
                    "reviewer": {
